.TH TOOLS9P 8
.SH NAME
tools9p \- serve a restricted Veltro tool and capability namespace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tools9p
[
.B -DvN
]
[
.B -a
.I activity
]
[
.B -r
.I role
]
[
.B -m
.I mountpoint
]
[
.B -b
.I tool,...
]
[
.B -p
.I path[:ro|:rw]
]
.I tool ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tools9p
serves the active Veltro tools and their effective namespace capabilities at
.BR /tool .
Only named tools exist. Each invocation receives a namespace constructed by
.IR nsconstruct .
.PP
The effective paths file uses records of the form
.IR "path ro|rw|cow" .
Activity scratch is always
.B /tmp/veltro/scratch cow
and is constructed specially. Passing that path with
.B -p
does not recursively grant or stage it. Tools and ordinary path capabilities
are selected explicitly on the command line; child provisioning can only
narrow the declared delegation budget.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -D
Enable 9P protocol tracing.
.TP
.B -v
Enable verbose server logging.
.TP
.B -N
Record that the agent namespace has NODEVS applied. This metadata must match
the namespace constructed by the trusted launcher.
.TP
.BI -a " activity"
Set the activity identity used for scratch and staged writes.
.TP
.BI -r " role"
Declare the audit role as
.B toplevel
or
.BR child .
.TP
.BI -m " mountpoint"
Serve somewhere other than
.BR /tool .
.TP
.BI -b " tool,..."
Set the maximum tool set that may be delegated to child tasks. Children can
narrow this set but cannot expand it.
.TP
.BI -p " path[:ro|:rw]"
Add an ordinary filesystem capability. Repeat as needed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
	tools9p -N read list find grep
	tools9p -N -p /mnt/msg:ro -p /mnt/msg/draft:rw read write
	nsaudit -m /tool
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /tmp/veltro/.ns/manifest
Effective restricted namespace manifest, sealed into the audit chain when
auditing is enabled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR nsaudit (1),
.IR namespace (6)
